<title>CANADA: WCE BARLEY BID C$5 LIMIT UP ON CBOT CORN SPILLOVER.</title>
<headline>WCE BARLEY BID C$5 LIMIT UP ON CBOT CORN SPILLOVER.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Winnipeg Commodity Exchange barley futures were bid up the $5.00-a-tonne limit on October and December contracts early, boosted by commission house short covering sparked by surging CBOT corn futures, traders said.</p>
<p>Floor sources noted LFG was among early buyers with the Alberta Wheat Pool a noted early seller.</p>
<p>At 0938 CDT October was bid up the C$5.00 limit at $137.10 a tonne.</p>
<p>((-Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
